            "title": "Steepening of U.S. Treasury Yield Curve Remains in Market's Focus",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "The focus in U.S. Treasurys is on the steepening yield curve as further Federal Reserve rate cuts are seen next year, Saxo's strategy team said in a note.  While the two-year benchmark Treasury yield remains anchored near 3.50%, the 10-year Treasury yield is hovering around close to the recent three-month high of just above 4.20%.  Last Friday, the yield spread between the 10-year and two-year Treasury yields closed above 66 basis points for the first time in 2025, the steepest the yield curve has been since early 2022, they said.",
